course: dictionary
lesson: 9246
title: The meaning of sorrow
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Sorrow is a noun. It means a deep feeling of sadness, often after a loss, a death or a disappointment. You can find its clues in the words around it. «She wept with sorrow when her grandmother died.» Wept and grandmother died tell you the sadness is deep and painful.
explain: A sorrow can also be a thing that makes you very sad. «Losing the final was one of his sorrows that year.» Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Try your meaning in the sentence instead of the hard word: one of his sad things still makes sense, so sorrow means a sad thing.
explain: In old or formal writing, sorrow can be a verb meaning to feel truly sorry for a wrong you did. Read the whole sentence before you decide. If the words talk about sin and forgiveness, sorrow means being sorry, not just being sad.
fact: Sorrow means a deep, heavy sadness, often after a loss, a death or a disappointment.
fact: «Drown your sorrows» means try to forget your sadness, often by drinking.
fact: «Joys and sorrows» means the happy and the sad times in life.
fact: Joel 2:13 says «Rend your heart and not your garments». Rend means tear, and people in Bible times tore their clothes to show sorrow, but God wants sorrow in the heart.
fact: «Crocodile tears» means pretend sorrow. Crocodiles can seem to cry while they eat, but this is probably air pushed through the head, not sadness.
exercise: «She felt great sorrow when her dog died.» What does sorrow mean here? | Great happiness | *Deep sadness | Hunger | A fast car
exercise: Which phrase means to try to forget your sadness, often by drinking? | Joys and sorrows | *Drown your sorrows | Rend your heart | Crocodile tears
exercise: «Crocodile tears» means what? | Real, deep sorrow | Happy laughter | *Pretend sorrow | Wet cheeks from the rain
test: Joel says «Rend your heart and not your garments». What does rend mean? | To wash | To mend | To hide | *To tear
test: «Her sorrow showed in her silence and her heavy heart.» What does this tell you about her? | *She felt deep sadness | She was asleep | She was hungry | She was very happy
exam: «David admitted his sin, and his prayer shows his sorrow for what he had done.» Here sorrow means: | Feeling hungry | *Feeling truly sorry for something wrong | Laughing at a funny joke | A petrol station
